# Keep secrets, data and local clutter out of the build context.
#
# This file is a security control, not housekeeping. Without it, COPY . .
# would bake .env (SECRET_KEY, ADMIN_PASSWORD, the LTI secret) and adsum.db
# (every student's name and attendance) into an image that people push to
# registries. Anything listed here cannot end up in a layer.

# Secrets and real data. The first three are the ones that matter.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
CREDENTIALS.txt
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
backups/
.migration-failed

# Version control and CI.
.git
.github
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Python local state.
.venv
venv
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
*.egg-info

# Editor and OS noise.
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Logs and scratch.
*.log
server.log
scratch/
tmp/

# Documentation and images are not needed at runtime and are the bulk of the
# tree. The image stays small and the docs stay on GitHub, where a reader
# can actually follow their links.
docs/
*.md
!README.md
